{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses hastened.</b> Once he heard the attributes that the Holy One, blessed be He, said — that He is compassionate and gracious and slow to anger — his mind was set at ease regarding what He said, ״פן אכלך״, and he gave thanks and bowed. And according to the one who explains, he went back and added prayer upon prayer: ״אם נא מצאתי חן בעיניך ילך נא״ etc. — that is, for that same reason that You said to us that You would not go, because ״עם קשה עורף אתה פן אכלך בדרך״ — for that same reason we need You to go with us, for it is a stiff-necked people, and You are El compassionate and gracious, and You forgive our iniquity and our sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:40.585560546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}